<BaseLayout title="Body and paint">
  <h1>Body and paint</h1>
  <h2>Paint identification</h2>
  <p>Paint names are not sufficient to identify a repair color. Confirm the factory paint code from the vehicle identification label before purchasing touch-up paint or arranging refinishing.</p>
  <h2>Minor paint scratches</h2>
  <p>First determine whether the mark is paint transfer, a clear-coat defect, or damage through the color coat. Clean and dry the area before inspection. A fingernail-catching scratch may extend beyond the clear coat and may require professional assessment.</p>
  <p>Do not use aggressive polishing compounds on an unknown finish or attempt to sand through the clear coat without appropriate experience and paint-thickness information.</p>
</BaseLayout>
